<rtept lat="52.3662840000" lon="-2.7310700000">
<time>2026-06-13T08:48:06Z</time>
<name>Lower Wood Road to End</name>
<desc><![CDATA[Keep ahead along Lower Wood Road for just 40 metres and then fork left to join the public footpath (signed as part of the Mortimer Trail long distance path). About 30 paces up the slope you will come to a fork (the left-hand branch being the one you came down on the outward leg). This time, take the right-hand branch, signed as a permissive route for the Mortimer Trail. 

Follow this pretty woodland trail, undulating and meandering along the woodland bank. After about 800 metres, the path swings left to reach a T-junction (with a waymarker post on your right). Turn left here (up the short slope) to reach the lay-by where the walk began. ]]></desc>
<sym>Flag</sym>
<type>Marks</type>
<extensions>
<xstyle:fill>
<xstyle:color>ff0000</xstyle:color>
</xstyle:fill>
</extensions>
</rtept>
