<rtept lat="52.3556220000" lon="-2.7509100000">
<time>2026-06-13T08:48:06Z</time>
<name>Viewpoint to Town View</name>
<desc><![CDATA[When you are ready to continue, stand with your back to the bench and view and walk forward for 10 paces (to draw level with the small brick building on your left). Turn right to continue your journey along the grass track. This track leads you down the slope to reach a junction with a surfaced forest road. Turn sharp left to join this road (heading uphill). 

At the brow of the rise, turn right to join a stone and grass vehicle track which leads you downhill. After just 80 metres, by a bench on your left, turn left to join a grass track leading you through the trees. Follow this unmade path, meandering ahead and narrowing (following the waymarker posts marked with red and green signs). 

As you approach the edge of the forest, join the compacted stone path which bends left. Where the stone path ends, continue straight ahead to reach the next waymarker post alongside a simple bench with your first views of Ludlow town ahead. ]]></desc>
<sym>Flag</sym>
<type>Marks</type>
